{"stats":{"took":77,"total":113,"estimate":false,"maxScore":284.8081},"results":[{"_meta":{"score":284.8081},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20130009147,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"cab0c5d3eed14b71a358e6eff86b2066","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Space Communications, Spacecraft Communications, Command And Tracking"],"keywords":["Deep Space Network","scheduling","optimization"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20130009147,"ear":"NO","id":"c1eb66e7c29444b284cf3750991c8513","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"Automating Mid- and Long-Range Scheduling for the NASA Deep Space Network","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-27T11:27:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20130009147,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark D."},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"321076879b2948e58f4edb9e4d22dcfe"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20130009147,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Tran, Daniel"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"2764caebece84f13b10ef6807c56edd7"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20130009147,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"hdl:2014/42580","submissionId":20130009147,"id":"61fd6d4e8b4945e3b7f112e2bfe43c10","type":"HANDLE"},{"submissionId":20130009147,"id":"54be1207fc194310b44b2f5aa31d8484","descriptor":"hdl:2014/42580"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-27T11:27:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"NASA has recently deployed a new mid-range scheduling system for the antennas of the Deep Space Network (DSN), called Service Scheduling Software, or S(sup 3). This system was designed and deployed as a modern web application containing a central scheduling database integrated with a collaborative environment, exploiting the same technologies as social web applications but applied to a space operations context. This is highly relevant to the DSN domain since the network schedule of operations is developed in a peer-to-peer negotiation process among all users of the DSN. These users represent not only NASA's deep space missions, but also international partners and ground-based science and calibration users. The initial implementation of S(sup 3) is complete and the system has been operational since July 2011. This paper describes some key aspects of the S(sup 3) system and on the challenges of modeling complex scheduling requirements and the ongoing extension of S(sup 3) to encompass long-range planning, downtime analysis, and forecasting, as the next step in developing a single integrated DSN scheduling tool suite to cover all time ranges.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","meetings":[{"submissionId":20130009147,"name":"European Space Agency","location":"Toulouse, France","id":"be890c13fa734995b943a238b0075e50"},{"country":"Italy","submissionId":20130009147,"endDate":"2012-09-06T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"meta":{"organization":{"name":"European Space Agency","location":"Toulouse, France"}},"meetingId":"a809398bb6e246288a755cf216a7bd0d","id":"3ef3cf1f2e5a4732a49a7489cb6d09a9"}],"name":"International Symposium on Artificial Intelligence, Robotics and Automation in Space","location":"Turin","id":"a809398bb6e246288a755cf216a7bd0d","startDate":"2012-09-04T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20130009147,"id":"d7395557d61e462c9a0921b62d8db531","publicationDate":"2012-09-04T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":277.83823},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20060042856,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"d0c50b8e4856421786c47d5119d76d0d","belongsToAuthors":false},"keywords":["conflict resolution","scheduling","Deep Space Network (DSN)"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20060042856,"ear":"NO","id":"c270a2faffd040f89676db353824e939","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"Automating Deep Space Network scheduling and conflict resolution","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-23T18:37:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20060042856,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark D."},"organization":{}},"id":"c93ce607f76444f89b3725aca16f3ec4"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20060042856,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Clement, Bradley"},"organization":{}},"id":"637772c03ec24289be702abd20c0ebca"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20060042856,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"hdl:2014/37775","submissionId":20060042856,"id":"350a11b49ecb4773bfe7998a58d0ee18","type":"HANDLE"},{"submissionId":20060042856,"id":"4348cf9ee1b846ebb43655246333926b","descriptor":"hdl:2014/37775"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-23T18:37:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The Deep Space Network (DSN) is a central part of NASA's infrastructure for communicating with active space missions, from earth orbit to beyond the solar system.  We describe our  recent work in modeling the complexities of user requirements, and then scheduling and resolving conflicts on that basis.  We emphasize our innovative use of background 'intelligent'  assistants' that carry out search asynchrnously while the user is focusing on various aspects of the schedule.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","meetings":[{"country":"Germany","submissionId":20060042856,"name":"i-SAIRAS","location":"Munich","id":"a28c62fca65b4fcfb1896fdb2ee65f86","startDate":"2005-09-05T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20060042856,"id":"fa05d6d4ae1d4764a9216357ee821966","publicationDate":"2005-09-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":265.0025},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20130009323,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"d17ae6bf95de4b85b00ab418d4eb7ea1","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Space Sciences (General)"],"keywords":["scheduling","Deep Space Network (DSN)","planning"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20130009323,"ear":"NO","id":"d6d7e39a0a89443dbbbed9ee01ee9e0b","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"Automating Mid- and Long-Range Scheduling for NASA's Deep Space Network","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-27T11:27:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark D."},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"8c2e01157aab40a9aa2e4ca7922622d0"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Tran, Daniel"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"3880a6d2e2334a77aaba82ef8d9525e9"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Arroyo, Belinda"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"6bf1eb36f6d94bfebf899e3f53183633"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Sorensen, Sugi"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"e087519a5e42455e9678b3ebdc3d4dfb"},{"sequence":4,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Tay, Peter"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"ddbbc0cd7a4a41dcb677e65de7ed647e"},{"sequence":5,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Carruth, Butch"},"organization":{"name":"Innovative Productivity Solutions, Inc.","location":"Bulverde, TX, United States"}},"id":"f3ced4de28a0427fa88cd82c43b0f00f"},{"sequence":6,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Coffman, Adam"},"organization":{"name":"Innovative Productivity Solutions, Inc.","location":"Bulverde, TX, United States"}},"id":"90a6df1b8929441f8075a0dcfc97316f"},{"sequence":7,"submissionId":20130009323,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Wallace, Mike"},"organization":{"name":"Innovative Productivity Solutions, Inc.","location":"Bulverde, TX, United States"}},"id":"0e05205b706f43ab846f86194026d5eb"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20130009323,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"hdl:2014/42582","submissionId":20130009323,"id":"4760d454f67b473b9e645f90a15dc659","type":"HANDLE"},{"submissionId":20130009323,"id":"72f7d8f502cc466581c779a3f9d6417d","descriptor":"hdl:2014/42582"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-27T11:27:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"NASA has recently deployed a new mid-range scheduling system for the antennas of the Deep Space Network (DSN), called Service Scheduling Software, or S(sup 3). This system is architected as a modern web application containing a central scheduling database integrated with a collaborative environment, exploiting the same technologies as social web applications but applied to a space operations context. This is highly relevant to the DSN domain since the network schedule of operations is developed in a peer-to-peer negotiation process among all users who utilize the DSN (representing 37 projects including international partners and ground-based science and calibration users). The initial implementation of S(sup 3) is complete and the system has been operational since July 2011. S(sup 3) has been used for negotiating schedules since April 2011, including the baseline schedules for three launching missions in late 2011. S(sup 3) supports a distributed scheduling model, in which changes can potentially be made by multiple users based on multiple schedule \"workspaces\" or versions of the schedule. This has led to several challenges in the design of the scheduling database, and of a change proposal workflow that allows users to concur with or to reject proposed schedule changes, and then counter-propose with alternative or additional suggested changes. This paper describes some key aspects of the S(sup 3) system and lessons learned from its operational deployment to date, focusing on the challenges of multi-user collaborative scheduling in a practical and mission-critical setting. We will also describe the ongoing project to extend S(sup 3) to encompass long-range planning, downtime analysis, and forecasting, as the next step in developing a single integrated DSN scheduling tool suite to cover all time ranges.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","meetings":[{"country":"Sweden","submissionId":20130009323,"endDate":"2012-06-15T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","name":"SpaceOps 2012","location":"Stockholm","id":"2c758747d4be4ac3965ab39c8aa3b572","startDate":"2012-06-11T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20130009323,"id":"e3514f400ce940f7ab86b986a78136da","publicationDate":"2012-06-11T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":260.35428},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20060042808,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"c4fe595c6a234009a16ca91b6aa32a9c","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Cybernetics, Artificial Intelligence And Robotics"],"keywords":["space communication","scheduling"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20060042808,"ear":"NO","id":"07dda4ae99d44d718724ead582f086e6","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"The Deep Space Network scheduling problem","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-23T18:37:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20060042808,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Clement, Bradley J."},"organization":{}},"id":"df2a56bf4c7a483880b30a1565902ee9"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20060042808,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark D."},"organization":{}},"id":"04254cc1ac534317ab796c31069ced7b"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20060042808,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"hdl:2014/37582","submissionId":20060042808,"id":"0635d5203cf643e194e559ad3cec5542","type":"HANDLE"},{"submissionId":20060042808,"id":"aa37dfe2bdd74e03a76717bcfb9c2426","descriptor":"hdl:2014/37582"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-23T18:37:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"We describe the Deep Space network's scheduling problem based on a user requriement language.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","meetings":[{"country":"United States","submissionId":20060042808,"name":"Innovative Applications of Artificial Intelligence 2005","location":"Pittsburgh, PA","id":"43c07851123f48299cb17cb66d485636","startDate":"2005-07-09T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20060042808,"id":"ea76d176c7c4490084aa6707653fc523","publicationDate":"2005-06-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":246.8945},"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"84A32425"},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19840049638,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"9d0cf26b1b3a4205ace75ff45d11e333","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Space Communications, Spacecraft Communications, Command And Tracking"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19840049638,"ear":"NO","id":"1fa299183c794f2789babbf990d37bcf","itar":"NO"},"created":"2013-08-12T02:40:00.0000000+00:00","distributionDate":"2011-08-17T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The functioning of the Deep Space Network Operations Scheduling, Jet Propulsion Laboratory, CA is reviewed. The primary objectives of the Operations Scheduling are: to schedule the worldwide global allocation of ground communications, tracking facilities, and equipment; and to provide deep space telecommunications for command, tracking, telemetry, and control in support of flight mission operations and tests. Elements of the earth set are Deep Space Stations (DSS) which provide the telecommunications link between the earth and spacecraft; NASA Communications Network; Network Data Processing Area; Network Operations Control Area which provides operational direction to the DSS; Mission Control and Computing systems; and Mission Support areas which provide flight control of the spacecraft. Elements of the space set include mission priorities and requirements which determine the spacecraft queue for allocating network resources. Scheduling is discussed in terms of long-range (3 years), mid-range (8 weeks), and short-range (2 weeks).","title":"NASA Deep Space Network Operations Scheduling","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-12T02:40:00.0000000+00:00","isLessonsLearned":false,"authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19840049638,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Enari, D. M."},"organization":{"name":"California Institute of Technology, Jet Propulsion Laboratory, Pasadena","location":"CA, United States"}},"id":"e53012ecf6e1489983b0b3ce80f65ff2"}],"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19840049638,"publications":[{"submissionId":19840049638,"id":"d3487041472d486ebbb5a8af2e7e1643","publicationDate":"1982-01-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":236.93958},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20070034024,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"bbd08163e9cc406c815476534323c369","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Statistics And Probability"],"keywords":["Deep Space Network (DSN)","scheduling","evolutionary computing"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20070034024,"ear":"NO","id":"a8e0f31139e04b6185c2f9e9f97a312c","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"Deep Space Network Scheduling Using Evolutionary Computational Methods","stiType":"PREPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-08-24T00:03:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20070034024,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Guillaume, Alexandre"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"ec438130a6f346cfacf961f68567c3bb"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20070034024,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Lee, Seugnwon"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"e191fff3a618460f8d252ce783c392e9"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20070034024,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Wang, Yeou-Fang"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"5c99e5bdb5e34790875bd6f946b83b6b"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20070034024,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Terrile, Richard J."},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"8cf931af25e74e8aa1195c4ce019a581"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Preprint (Draft being sent to journal)","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20070034024,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"hdl:2014/40315","submissionId":20070034024,"id":"b1b603468ada47eda0a7fd3cf7cea2fa","type":"HANDLE"},{"submissionId":20070034024,"id":"5b91a42b648c47488966e4b1fb317003","descriptor":"hdl:2014/40315"}],"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2013-08-24T00:03:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The paper presents the specific approach taken to formulate the problem in terms of gene encoding, fitness function, and genetic operations. The genome is encoded such that a subset of the scheduling constraints is automatically satisfied. Several fitness functions are formulated to emphasize different aspects of the scheduling problem. The optimal solutions of the different fitness functions demonstrate the trade-off of the scheduling problem and provide insight into a conflict resolution process.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","meetings":[{"submissionId":20070034024,"name":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers","location":"United States","id":"581ce14a50a9403da572f2c666179c39"},{"country":"United States","submissionId":20070034024,"endDate":"2007-03-10T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"meta":{"organization":{"name":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers","location":"United States"}},"meetingId":"2ae9b3966de143f09592e7624d5c3839","id":"adbb5436189f45719888f3622fb00391"}],"name":"IEEE Aerospace Conference","location":"Big Sky, MT","id":"2ae9b3966de143f09592e7624d5c3839","startDate":"2007-03-03T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20070034024,"id":"e958382d91a64014ab71b11fa5a8a645","publicationDate":"2007-03-03T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":222.95985},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"approverComments":"Items in TRS are protected by copyright, but are furnished with U.S. government purpose use rights.","containsIndication":true,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20210001350,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":true,"id":"552fdf8384c445e5a69079691bf7c557","belongsToAuthors":false},"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"UNSET","submissionId":20210001350,"ear":"UNSET","id":"948b9d4700d64c6ebbedc13b9effbf8d","itar":"UNSET"},"created":"2011-06-08T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","distributionDate":"2011-06-08T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":0,"abstract":"This paper describes the DSN Scheduling Engine (DSE) component of a new scheduling system being deployed for NASA’s Deep Space Network. The DSE provides core automation functionality for scheduling the network, including the interpretation of scheduling requirements expressed by users, their elaboration into tracking passes, and resolving conflicts and constraint violations. The DSE incorporates both systematic search and repair-based algorithms, used for different phases and  purposes in the overall system. It has been integrated in with a web application which provides its functionality to all DSN users through a standard web browser. The system is in the process of deployment to operational status.","title":"Automated scheduling for NASA’s Deep Space Network","stiType":"PREPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20210001350,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Tran, Daniel"}},"id":"ae49c2dd568f41c6bd8d6b908c5fa20a"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20210001350,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark D."}},"id":"0aec892080ed459e802371702ea66510"}],"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","stiTypeDetails":"Preprint (Draft being sent to journal)","technicalReviewType":"NOT_SET","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20210001350,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"2014/43478","submissionId":20210001350,"id":"397435b4e1954e8387c55ebc671bee44","type":"HANDLE"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20210001350,"publisher":"Pasadena, CA : Jet Propulsion Laboratory, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, 2011.","id":"6b3c61dc24724839929f5428fcd2c19a","publicationDate":"2011-06-08T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":215.10333},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19890000699,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"ed489df47313496caa0bf235523583ba","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Administration And Management"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19890000699,"ear":"NO","id":"c2efb4b2a5254851b63a78eddc8352a3","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2013-08-29T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","title":"Deep space network resource scheduling approach and application","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-09-05T18:59:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19890000699,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Eggemeyer, William C."},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"d90b466b66bc4e628863ed75dd099004"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":19890000699,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Bowling, Alan"},"organization":{"name":"Jet Propulsion Lab., California Inst. of Tech.","location":"Pasadena, CA, United States"}},"id":"ca01b791067f489598ccfca3b65578a5"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19890000699,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"89N10070"},"created":"2013-09-05T18:59:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"Deep Space Network (DSN) resource scheduling is the process of distributing ground-based facilities to track multiple spacecraft. The Jet Propulsion Laboratory has carried out extensive research to find ways of automating this process in an effort to reduce time and manpower costs. This paper presents a resource-scheduling system entitled PLAN-IT with a description of its design philosophy. The PLAN-IT's current on-line usage and limitations in scheduling the resources of the DSN are discussed, along with potential enhancements for DSN application.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19890000699,"id":"87583ef09e294992af125964d1a993cf","publicationName":"NASA, Goddard Space Flight Center, Proceedings of 1987 Goddard Conference on Space Applications of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Robotics","publicationDate":"1987-01-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19890000699.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19890000699/downloads/19890000699.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19890000699/downloads/19890000699.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19890000699/downloads/19890000699.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":211.36607},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"approverComments":"Items in TRS are protected by copyright, but are furnished with U.S. government purpose use rights.","containsIndication":true,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20230005625,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":true,"id":"5a5d0845a3be47af8eb8d31478591561","belongsToAuthors":false},"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"UNSET","submissionId":20230005625,"ear":"UNSET","id":"e6c0c3022516493bb63e88ca2eb59ad0","itar":"UNSET"},"created":"2021-07-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","distributionDate":"2021-07-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":0,"abstract":"NASA’s Deep Space Network (DSN) is a mission critical facility that supports many different space missions,from LEO to deep space exploration. In recent years, as the network has suffered from increasing oversubscription, more restrictions have been added to reduce the amount of manual scheduling labor necessary to come to consensus. In this paper, we describe a new auto-mated scheduling tool which takes advantage of these restrictions to bring the scheduling problem closer to feasibility. In addition, we describe an algorithm to reduce problem inputs given a partially-solved problem,thereby bringing the problem even closer to feasibility","title":"Utilizing Schedule Constraints to Improve Automated Scheduling in NASA's Deep Space Network","stiType":"PREPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230005625,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnston, Mark"}},"id":"b070e77a02c649d3bb4a0bebc7c79f01"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230005625,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Troesch, Martina"}},"id":"918e30ba99b643779b708671bdc58c00"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230005625,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Dhamani, Nihal"}},"id":"f876467426044a80845e5ed26b5336cc"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230005625,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Davis, Evan W"}},"id":"827c5976c69a43d9b115c06ecb304f6f"}],"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","stiTypeDetails":"Preprint (Draft being sent to journal)","technicalReviewType":"NOT_SET","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20230005625,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"2014/55084","submissionId":20230005625,"id":"20b2b53e9f384205b3a597dc17e79047","type":"HANDLE"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20230005625,"publisher":"Pasadena, CA: Jet Propulsion Laboratory, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, 2021","id":"b41180a8d0944b0cb0e45e5253fd56e3","publicationDate":"2021-07-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"},{"_meta":{"score":204.52621},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"approverComments":"Items in TRS are protected by copyright, but are furnished with U.S. government purpose use rights.","containsIndication":true,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20220003798,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":true,"id":"200a58a9d7554f298a8bd35545c8f3d1","belongsToAuthors":false},"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"UNSET","submissionId":20220003798,"ear":"UNSET","id":"e4a049aaed3a4cfda0077e24d5af6825","itar":"UNSET"},"created":"2021-03-06T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","distributionDate":"2021-03-06T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":0,"abstract":"With three complexes spread evenly across the Earth, NASA’s Deep Space Network (DSN) is the primary means of communications as well as a significant scientific instrument for dozens of active missions around the world. A rapidly rising number of spacecraft and increasingly complex scientific instruments with higher bandwidth requirements have resulted in demand that exceeds the network’s capacity across its 12 antennae. The existing DSN scheduling process operates on a rolling weekly basis and is time-consuming; for a given week, generation of the final baseline schedule of spacecraft tracking passes takes roughly 5 months from the initial requirements submission deadline, with several weeks of peer-to-peer negotiations in between. This paper proposes a deep reinforcement learning (RL) approach to generate candidate DSN schedules from mission requests and spacecraft ephemeris data with demonstrated capability to address real-world operational constraints. A deep RL agent is developed that takes mission requests for a given week as input, and interacts with a DSN scheduling environment to allocate tracks such that its reward signal is maximized. A comparison is made between an agent trained using Proximal Policy Optimization and its random, untrained counterpart. The results represent a proof-of-concept that, given a well-shaped reward signal, a deep RL agent can learn the complex heuristics used by experts to schedule the DSN. A trained agent can potentially be used to generate candidate schedules to bootstrap the scheduling process and thus reduce the turnaround cycle for DSN scheduling.","title":"Scheduling the NASA Deep Space Network with Deep Reinforcement Learning","stiType":"PREPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20220003798,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Wilson, Brian"}},"id":"708ccd60cddb41b6a860be437742aa0e"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20220003798,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Hoffmann, Mark"}},"id":"9287facb023f435e89c409b91548868e"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20220003798,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Venkataram, Hamsa"}},"id":"7b7c49bf551c41189d568efda3835564"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20220003798,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Goh, Edwin Y"}},"id":"2a8a26473d5f41f1a4aae51a666acf6b"}],"disseminated":"METADATA_ONLY","stiTypeDetails":"Preprint (Draft being sent to journal)","technicalReviewType":"NOT_SET","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20220003798,"sourceIdentifiers":[{"number":"2014/54269","submissionId":20220003798,"id":"9e3cb7d714444423a31b4376a0a9dfd7","type":"HANDLE"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20220003798,"publisher":"Pasadena, CA: Jet Propulsion Laboratory, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, 2021","id":"8df2ed801cb44218a93f1fba95c948b3","publicationDate":"2021-03-06T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[],"downloadsAvailable":false,"index":"submissions-2026-11-12-06-24"}],"aggregations":{"created":{"buckets":[{"key_as_string":"2013","key":1356998400000,"doc_count":66},{"key_as_string":"2015","key":1420070400000,"doc_count":8},{"key_as_string":"2021","key":1609459200000,"doc_count":7},